FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/formatter.rs:341 — `Unless` uses `self.newline()` instead of `open_line(stmt.span.line)` — a trailing comment on `unless cond then // note` is not claimed on the opener, so `format_statements` later emits it inside the block or `write_trailing_comment` re-attaches it to the `end` line, migrating the comment off the line its author wrote — change to `self.open_line(stmt.span.line)` like `If`/`ForEach`/`While`/`Try`.
2. [MAJOR] src/formatter.rs:452 — `Module` uses `self.newline()` instead of `open_line(stmt.span.line)` — same migration: `module Name // note` is emitted as a leading comment in the body or trailing `end // note` after `format_block` advances `last_line` to the `end` line — change to `self.open_line(stmt.span.line)`.
3. [MINOR] src/formatter.rs:823 — doc claims `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` and `in` have no token and cannot reach the formatter — false on this tree: `Lexer` produces `Less`/`LessEqual`/`Greater`/`GreaterEqual`/`In` (src/lexer.rs:99,145) and `Parser` builds them, so the comment misdescribes reachable spellings — rewrite the doc to state both spellings are grammar and the formatter normalises to the symbolic form.
4. [MAJOR] tests/formatter_test.rs:15 — `corpus()` does `let Ok(entries) = fs::read_dir(&path) else { continue; }`, silently skipping a missing `examples`/`tests`/`modules` dir while only asserting the total is non-empty — a deleted or renamed `modules/` still passes with reduced coverage, weakening the idempotence/losslessness properties the phase claims over all three dirs — fail loudly per-dir or assert each dir contributed files.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
